      "summary": "Spain has opened several housing centers in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta to accommodate approximately 1800 migrants currently present in the territory, with specific provisions being made for around 500 unaccompanied minors who are being taken into care as part of efforts to address the humanitarian crisis in the region.",
